  "text" : "You can change what your classifier does without retraining it.\nIt's a prompt injection detector.\nYou just move this line.\nAn ROC curve shows every place that you could put it.\nThe model doesn't say yes or no. It gives every request a score.\nAnd this threshold is what turns that score into a yes.\nYou slide it to the left and we can catch every attack.\nBut we end up blocking most of our users.\nIf you slide it to the right, almost nobody gets blocked,\nbut half of the attacks get through.\nEvery threshold gives a new confusion matrix,\nand each one is a point.\npositive rate up, false positive rate across. Top left is the sweet spot. Now ROC is for\npicking thresholds. You decide whether you'd rather avoid false positives or get all the\npositives depending on the problem you're solving."
}
